# Every pressed layer whose absorbing buffer is sized and whose served shares are all stated,
# beside what it was asked to hold. One row per layer examined, `violates` where the whole range of
# the shares is above the whole slack.
#
# A share fits inside its buffer
#   The rule: a share does not exceed the slack of the buffer that absorbed it. The remainder names
#   an absorber, the absorber names a buffer, and the buffer has a size. Shares attributed to it
#   have to fit inside it, which is what makes a buffer a quantity rather than a label.
#
# Three answers, as checks/draw_exceeds_the_supply.sqlc gives them
#   The shares and the slack are both ranges. The whole range of the shares fits inside the
#   smallest slack, or the two ranges overlap, or the whole range of the shares is above the
#   largest slack. The most likely values decide none of the three.
#
# Only an excess across the whole range is a violation
#   The smallest load above the largest slack is a filing error with no defence. Ranges that
#   overlap are a document that cannot settle its own question, and reporting that as a breach
#   would accuse a filer of something their figures do not say. `detail` says which of the three a
#   row is.
#
# `customer` and `unrealised` are exempt
#   They are the overflow rather than a load, and a `transition` layer is not examined at all;
#   entries/borne.sqlc gives the reasons for both. Exempting `unrealised` alone is not enough:
#   where a filing states a capacity of zero, as `refutation/compute` does, the comparison would
#   read a share from the clearance side against a bound from the interference side.
#
# One unstated share leaves the layer unexamined
#   A share filed `unmeasured`, or as `sharesSum`'s output, is not in the sum, so a layer carrying
#   one adds up to less than the buffer holds. A sum that fits shows nothing then, and a passing
#   verdict would be the check supplying the missing share as zero. So the layer is left out, as
#   checks/shares_do_not_sum.sqlc and checks/exposure_unaccounted.sqlc leave theirs, and
#   arithmetic/shares_bounded.sqlc says it is suspended.
-- pm:Remainder/pm:holder against the three slack elements, keyed by pm:Remainder/pm:absorber
-- through pm.buffer_term.
SELECT r.rule, p.filing, p.layer, p.violates, p.detail
FROM      (
    :compose(checks/roster.sqlc)
) r
LEFT JOIN (
    SELECT b.filing, b.layer,
           -- the smallest load above the largest slack
           coalesce(b.borne_low > b.slack_high + 1e-9, false)          AS violates,
           CASE WHEN b.borne_low  > b.slack_high + 1e-9
                THEN format('[%s, %s] attributed to the %s buffer, whose slack is at most %s: '
                            'the whole range is over the line',
                            b.borne_low, b.borne_high, b.buffer, b.slack_high)
                WHEN b.borne_high <= b.slack_low + 1e-9
                THEN format('[%s, %s] attributed to the %s buffer, whose slack is at least %s: '
                            'the whole range clears',
                            b.borne_low, b.borne_high, b.buffer, b.slack_low)
                ELSE format('[%s, %s] attributed to the %s buffer, whose slack is [%s, %s]: the '
                            'ranges overlap, so this document does not settle whether the buffer '
                            'was overrun',
                            b.borne_low, b.borne_high, b.buffer, b.slack_low, b.slack_high)
           END                                                         AS detail
    FROM (
        :compose(entries/borne.sqlc)
    ) b
    WHERE b.unstated = 0
) p ON true
WHERE r.slug = 'share_exceeds_slack'
